# SleepKnight8 Themes

A simple theme library for SleepKnight8 projects.

## Setup

### 1. Copy the files

Copy these two files into your project:

```text
SleepKnight8_Themes.css
SleepKnight8_Themes.js
```

### 2. Add the CSS

Inside `<head>`:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="SleepKnight8_Themes.css">
```

### 3. Add the theme class

Change your `<body>` to:

```html
<body class="sleepknight8-theme">
```

### 4. Add the JavaScript

Before `</body>`:

```html
<script src="SleepKnight8_Themes.js"></script>
```

### 5. Add theme buttons

Use these wherever you want:

```html
<button onclick="setTheme('yellow')">🟡</button>
<button onclick="setTheme('purple')">🟣</button>
```

### 6. Make your layout

You can design your HTML however you want. The library handles the theme, while **your project controls the layout and functionality**.

### Complete example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>My Project</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="SleepKnight8_Themes.css">
</head>

<body class="sleepknight8-theme">

    <h1>My Project</h1>

    <button onclick="setTheme('yellow')">🟡</button>
    <button onclick="setTheme('purple')">🟣</button>

    <!-- Your own layout goes here -->

    <script src="SleepKnight8_Themes.js"></script>

</body>

</html>
```

**That's it.** You can completely change the layout without breaking the theme.
